  <note><content>
    <p>RK26 is a retrospective data-adequacy audit, not a preregistered mechanism experiment. The source is the MAGE-seq codon-pair assay, https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5234859/. The formal production read only codon1, aa1, pos1, codon2, aa2, pos2 and is_wt. Fitness, expression, RCS, MFE, RBS and SD-like fields were excluded from the derived fact table. Raw source SHA256 is 873f4ef0b410fb1299217d7c5cf0ffd5c78947591c9f944da867c428bdf93672; clean source SHA256 is 7acecf37b7ca432468a8e5c7a45ab6f471df41ae7d30d493cf8e4fe95e06edf1.</p>
    <p>The raw table contains 8,192 rows: two WT controls, 252 single-codon variants in the pair assay and 7,938 codon-pair variants. Fixed-protein identity was reconstructed with the standard genetic code from the unique WT row in each pair context. Only 6 synonymous single-codon variants and 4 synonymous double-codon variants remain. Pair 1–2 has WT GCC;AAA, 4 synonymous singles and 3 synonymous doubles. Pair 2–3 has WT AAA;GAA, 2 synonymous singles and 1 synonymous double. All 8,192 raw rows and all 8,192 clean metadata rows reconcile exactly.</p>
    <p>The frozen feasibility rule requires at least two synonymous singles and two synonymous doubles in each pair context. Pair 1–2 passes; pair 2–3 fails because it has only one double. This is a design-feasibility rule, not a power analysis. The resulting decision is FIXED_PROTEIN_SINGLE_TO_DOUBLE_SYNONYMOUS_OOD_NOT_SUPPORTED_BY_SAMPLE_COVERAGE. Four double-synonymous constructs may support descriptive biology, but not the proposed confirmatory cross-context OOD model comparison.</p>
    <p>No model was fitted, no functional endpoint was evaluated, and no confidence interval or p-value was produced. The original MAGE 33-construct mechanism test and the RK04 functional-untouched split were not accessed. This audit does not support protein-OOD, velocity, decay, spatial-coupling, CodonFlow-RK superiority, external SOTA or generator claims. RK-G1 remains false and generator training remains unauthorized.</p>
    <p>Synthetic tests passed 10 of 10, independent raw-source verification passed 42 of 42, and closeout evidence binding passed 54 of 54. Sequence-only fact artifact SHA256 is ad96263a513c986abcd62b71c7927704b927422be383dc5bc71d60abc4c4b531. Production result SHA256 is 264d6a6dd4df2cd52738f9f465d6d0bcc67bb9784cb59304e733d7f55f519851; independent report SHA256 is 5a61826999015bc448636812e104ed0ff84a20f21b5efc522bf7be5a636632f0. Science closeout commit is 6c142514701188efc7cdf79dd99eaf637685434c; registry closeout commit is 09338fb1fb834c72550ad509db2a4692daa97969.</p>
  </content></note>
